# This file is used to configure the behavior of web server when a file is not
# found, if no files match the <url> request, and the request is not a directory.
# The last rule in this file catches all requests and serves the index.html file
# so that the client-side routing can work properly.

# This allows client-side routing to work properly
# All requests that don't match a file or directory will be served index.html
# This is necessary for React Router to work correctly

# Serve index.html for all routes
# This enables client-side routing
# Without this, refreshing the page on a route like /chat would result in a 404

# The order of these rules matters:
# 1. First, try to serve the requested file
# 2. If the file doesn't exist, serve index.html
# 3. This allows React Router to handle the routing

# This is a standard configuration for single-page applications
# It ensures that all routes are handled by the React application
# rather than the web server trying to find physical files

# Note: This file is used by the development server and build process
# It's automatically included when using react-scripts
